  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Delta Canis Majoris",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Canis Major",
    "summary": "Delta Canis Majoris is a supergiant star in the constellation of Canis Major. It is formally named Wezen ; Delta Canis Majoris is its Bayer designation. At an apparent magnitude of +1.83, it is the third-brightest star in the constellation. Based on parallax measurements, it is located at a distance of approximately 1,600 light years. Since 1943, the spectrum of this star has served as one of the stable anchor points by which other stars are classified.",
    "intro": "Delta Canis Majoris is a supergiant star in the constellation of Canis Major. It is formally named Wezen (); Delta Canis Majoris is its Bayer designation. At an apparent magnitude of +1.83, it is the third-brightest star in the constellation. Based on parallax measurements, it is located at a distance of approximately 1,600 light years. Since 1943, the spectrum of this star has served as one of the stable anchor points by which other stars are classified.",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delta_Canis_Majoris",
